(a) Application for a license under this article shall be made as provided in chapter 12, except that such application shall contain the following additional information:
(1) The financial status of the applicant, including the amounts of all unpaid judgments against the applicant and the nature of the transaction or acts giving rise to said judgments;
(2) The experience of the applicant in the transportation of passengers;
(3) Any facts that the applicant believes tend to prove that public convenience and necessity require the granting of a license;
(4) The number of vehicles to be operated or controlled by the applicant and the location of proposed depots and terminals; and
(5) The color scheme or insignia to be used to designate the vehicle or vehicles of the applicant.
(b) All applicants shall also submit to a background check of their criminal history through the Georgia Crime Information Center and of their driving history with the Georgia Department of Driver Services.
